Priority badges, which must differ from each other in the count
and not only in the tone:
  Urgent bars 4 of 4  tone 4
  High bars 3 of 4  tone 3
  Medium bars 2 of 4  tone 3
  Low bars 1 of 4  tone 1
  None bars 0 of 4  tone 5

High and Medium are both tone-warning, so the count is the ONLY
thing that separates them and this row is the one that fails if
the bars stop being carried:
  High bars 3 against Medium bars 2

  distinct bar counts over the five priorities: 5 of 5

Controls. A status dot carries no quantity and must stay a custom
node, so these read -1 and no gauge leaked into them:
  status 0 gauge value -1
  status 4 gauge value -1
  label pill gauge value -1

The tone must survive the change of kind, since that is what the
renderers resolve the colour through:
  Urgent tone 4  must be tone-error 4
  None tone   5  must be tone-muted 5
